    "Dry Bulk Freight": "Capesize: The Capesize C5TC average declined by USD 2.8k/day closing the week at USD 48,812/ day. Trip from Continent to F.East is down by 0.3k/day at USD 87,333/day, Transatlantic R/V is lower by 1.6k/day at USD 54,750/day, and Bolivar to Rotterdam is lower by 2.2k/day at USD 61,232/ day, while Transpacific R/V is reduced by 7k/day at USD 50,341/day. Trip from Tubarao to Rotter- dam is reduced by 1k/day at USD 44,083/day, Chi- na-Brazil R/V is higher by 0.6k/day at USD 51,379/ day, and trip from Saldanha Bay to Qinqdao is re- duced by 1k/day at USD 44,083/day.\n\nKamsarmax/Panamax: The Kamsarmax P5TC Timecharter average started the week at USD 21,662/day closing with a decline at USD 20,262/ day. Trip from Skaw-Gib to F.East is softer by 1.1k/ day at USD 29,598/day, Pacific R/V is down by 1.8k/day at USD 20,400/day, while Transatlantic R/V is reduced by 1.2k/day at USD 18,859/day, and Singapore R/V via Atlantic is decreased by 1.7k/day at USD 20,640/day.\n\nUltramax/Supramax: The Ultramax S11TC average closed the week about USD 0.6k/day higher than its opening at USD 22,332/day. The Supramax S10TC average closed the week about 0.6k/day higher than its opening at USD 20,298/day. The Baltic Su- pramax Asia S3TC average closed the week about 0.9k/day higher than previous week at USD 20,802/ day. N. China one Australian or Pacific R/V is im- proved by 0.9k/day at USD 20,919/day, USG to Skaw Passero is softer by 0.3k/day at USD 32,763/ day. S. China trip via Indonesia to EC India is up by 1.6k/day at USD 25,229/day, trip from S. China via Indonesia to S. China pays USD 16,206/day, while Med/B.Sea to China/S.Korea is increased by 1k/day at USD 25,621/day.\n\nHandysize: The Handysize HS7TC average closed the week improved by 0.9k/day at USD 17,776/day. Skaw-Passero trip to Boston-Galveston pays 0.5k/ day more at USD 12,700/day, Brazil to Cont. pays 0.9k/day more at USD 25,167/day, S.E. Asia trip to Spore/Japan 0.2k/day is softer at USD 18,044/day,